  "name": "canonical_json",
  "notes": "json.dumps(obj, sort_keys=True, separators=(',', ':'), ensure_ascii=False): the card hash input. Floats use Python repr (shortest round-trip; exponent form when exp < -4 or >= 16, written like 1e-05 / 1e+16; integral floats keep '.0'). Keys sort by code point (= UTF-8 byte order). Only \" \\\\ and U+0000..U+001F are escaped (\\n \\r \\t \\b \\f short forms, others \\u00xx lowercase); U+007F, U+2028 and non-ASCII are written raw. NaN/Infinity and ints outside i64/u64 are not representable in the vector files and are left out.",
